There was a possible problems witch cache coherency when allocating memory from "uncached" zone. I.e. with SOF_MEM_ZONE_RUNTIME_SHARED flag set. In that case heap_alloc_aligned was called directly and alignment was not set.

	if (zone_is_cached(zone) && !(flags & SOF_MEM_FLAG_COHERENT)) {
		ptr = (__sparse_force void *)heap_alloc_aligned_cached(heap, 0, bytes);
	} else {
		ptr = heap_alloc_aligned(heap, PLATFORM_DCACHE_ALIGN, bytes);
	}

Any following cache invalidation on secondary cores may lead to issues.

